From: Droidspaces Builder <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] old-kernel: tolerate Android 4.14 network and cgroup behavior

Android kernels older than 5.3 reject RTM_GETNEXTHOP with EINVAL even when
systemd is built without SELinux support. Treat that result like
EOPNOTSUPP so networkd can continue without nexthop objects.

Containers cannot change the host kernel command line. When systemd can
already identify that it runs in a container, allow it to use the existing
cgroup v1 hierarchy without requiring SYSTEMD_CGROUP_ENABLE_LEGACY_FORCE.

---
 src/network/networkd-manager.c | 2 +-
 src/shared/cgroup-setup.c       | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/network/networkd-manager.c b/src/network/networkd-manager.c
index 6f1d73d..089bed0 100644
--- a/src/network/networkd-manager.c
+++ b/src/network/networkd-manager.c
@@ -1078,7 +1078,7 @@ static int manager_enumerate(Manager *m) {
         /* NextHop support is added in kernel v5.3 (65ee00a9409f751188a8cdc0988167858eb4a536),
          * and older kernels return -EOPNOTSUPP, or -EINVAL if SELinux is enabled. */
         r = manager_enumerate_nexthop(m);
-        if (r == -EOPNOTSUPP || (r == -EINVAL && mac_selinux_enforcing()))
+        if (IN_SET(r, -EOPNOTSUPP, -EINVAL))
                 log_debug_errno(r, "Could not enumerate nexthops, ignoring: %m");
         else if (r < 0)
                 return log_error_errno(r, "Could not enumerate nexthops: %m");
diff --git a/src/shared/cgroup-setup.c b/src/shared/cgroup-setup.c
index 36493dd..5659d2a 100644
--- a/src/shared/cgroup-setup.c
+++ b/src/shared/cgroup-setup.c
@@ -164,6 +164,10 @@ bool cg_is_legacy_force_enabled(void) {
         int r;
         bool b;
 
+        /* A container cannot add flags to the host kernel command line. */
+        if (detect_container() > 0)
+                return true;
+
         /* Require both systemd.unified_cgroup_hierarchy=0 and SYSTEMD_CGROUP_ENABLE_LEGACY_FORCE=1. */
 
         if (!cg_is_legacy_enabled())
